From 3ceec30faa7d8c8889caf5bb02062dc2ae648f20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:51:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] One-shot collectives: startup waits as long as its
 rendezvous; profiling names a stopped collective

Kernels still JIT-compile inside memory profiling and warm-up, for as long
as each rank's cache needs. The rendezvous lines ranks up at the entrance,
but a rank whose cache is warm then waits in the next collective for one
that is compiling, and the serving wait (10 s) stops the GPU there. With one
rank's TileLang cache cold, r6s traps in profile_run every time: rank 0 waits
for rank 1's attention-metadata compiles, Xid 43, and the error reads
cuModuleLoadData CUDA_ERROR_LAUNCH_FAILED. Every failed start leaves the
torn-down ranks further behind, so it repeats.

- Startup's one-shot collectives wait as long as the startup rendezvous
  (VLLM_STARTUP_RENDEZVOUS_TIMEOUT_MS) from the communicators' creation; the
  serving wait (SPARKNET_ROCE_TIMEOUT_MS) returns once warm-up is done, before
  the JIT monitor starts. A stopped collective still stops the GPU.
- Memory profiling and warm-up re-raise a CUDA error as the stopped
  collective's report, as execute_model and sample_tokens do: profile_run
  calls the model runner directly, outside those wrappers.

Needs sparknet's SparknetOneShotAllReduce.set_timeout_ms.

Reported-by: huxiaofengtiger (NVIDIA Developer Forums, DeepSeek 4.1 Flash recipe thread, post 24)
